Requirements: 25   with obligations: 24   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] A repeated review changes a criterion's test-evidence rating only when
    something that criterion depends on has changed, and says what that change was.
    -> repeated-review-conditional-rating-update  [functional/explicit]
       A repeated review changes a criterion's test-evidence rating only when that
       criterion's dependencies have changed, and it reports what change occurred.
    -> repeated-review-change-explanation  [functional/explicit]
       A repeated review reports the change to a criterion's dependencies that its
       rating change rests on.

[constraint-01] A review that has no stored earlier review judges every criterion
    without reference to an earlier rating.
    -> no-stored-earlier-review-judges-each-criterion-fresh  [functional/explicit]
       A review with no stored earlier review judges every criterion without reference
       to an earlier rating.

[constraint-02] A repeated review matches each criterion to the stored review's
    criterion for the same requirement, by something that does not move between runs.
    -> stable-criterion-matching-for-repeated-review  [functional/explicit]
       A repeated review matches each criterion to the stored review's criterion for the
       same requirement by something that does not move between runs.

[constraint-03] A criterion depends on its requirement text, the set of tests mapped to
    it, and the content of those tests.
    -> criterion-dependency-set  [invariant/explicit]
       A criterion depends on its requirement text, the set of tests mapped to it, and
       the content of those tests.

[constraint-04] When a repeated review finds a criterion's dependencies unchanged, it
    carries that criterion's stored test-evidence rating forward and makes no model call
    for it.
    -> carry-forward-unchanged-rating-without-model-call  [functional/explicit]
       When a repeated review finds a criterion's dependencies unchanged, it carries
       that criterion's stored test-evidence rating forward and makes no model call for
       it.

[constraint-05] When a repeated review finds a criterion's dependencies changed, it
    judges that criterion again, and the judgement is given the stored rating and the
    changes.
    -> rejudge-changed-dependencies-with-stored-rating-and-changes  [functional/explicit]
       When a repeated review finds a criterion's dependencies changed, it judges that
       criterion again, and the judgement is given the stored rating and the changes.

[constraint-06] A repeated judgement that alters a criterion's rating gives a reason,
    and names the change to that criterion's dependencies the reason rests on.
    -> changed-rating-explains-dependency-change  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       A repeated judgement that alters a criterion's rating gives a reason, and names
       the change to that criterion's dependencies the reason rests on.

[constraint-07] The change a repeated judgement names is one of the changes it was
    given.
    -> named-change-must-come-from-given-changes  [invariant/explicit]
       The change a repeated judgement names is one of the changes it was given.

[constraint-08] The stored earlier review is an input to a repeated review, and two
    repeated reviews from the same stored review and the same inputs produce byte-
    identical review state.
    -> stored-earlier-review-input-and-byte-identical-state  [compatibility/explicit]
       The stored earlier review is an input to a repeated review, and two repeated
       reviews from the same stored review and the same inputs produce byte-identical
       review state.

[constraint-09] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-no-live-model-calls  [functional/explicit]
       Tests avoid live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Which tests are discovered, and which criteria they are mapped to, which
    is #182.
    -> exclude-discovery-and-mapping-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are discovered or which criteria they are
       mapped to.

[exclusion-02] Whether a mapping change must likewise be explained, which is #182.
    -> exclude-mapping-change-explanation-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not require explaining a mapping change.

[exclusion-03] How many plausible defects a criterion's judgement names, and whether a
    rating requires every one of them to be caught, which is #183.
    -> exclude-plausible-defects-count-and-catch-all-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how many plausible defects a criterion's judgement
       names or whether a rating requires every one of them to be caught.

[exclusion-04] Whether a rating that could not be reproduced is reported as
    unreproducible.
    -> exclude-unreproducible-reporting-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether a rating that could not be reproduced is
       reported as unreproducible.

[exclusion-05] Whether a carried-forward rating is shown differently from a freshly
    judged one.
    -> exclude-carried-forward-vs-freshly-judged-display-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether a carried-forward rating is shown differently
       from a freshly judged one.

[exclusion-06] Whether the controls that make a run reproducible are consolidated into a
    single component, which is #184.
    -> exclude-reproducibility-controls-consolidation-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether the controls that make a run reproducible are
       consolidated into a single component.

[exclusion-07] Assigning obligation types, which is #205.
    -> exclude-obligation-type-assignment-scope  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter assigning obligation types.

